    812  f0e2							; --- VDEL: P0 ON, P1 OFF. NOT the HUD's 13+2 usage — this is the cave's
    813  f0e2							; one-line-ahead discipline, and it is x-INDEPENDENT only when the landing
    814  f0e2							; point of the write is RIGHT of every sprite pixel.
    815  f0e2							; Facts (Stella `Player::grp` / `updatePattern`): without VDEL a GRP write
    816  f0e2							; lands in `myPatternNew` and is rendered immediately, so a mid-line write
    817  f0e2							; affects the CURRENT line when the sprite has not started yet (its pixels
    818  f0e2							; begin at cycle ~(61+X)/3) and the NEXT line otherwise. `myPatternOld`,
    819  f0e2							; the VDEL slot, is latched when the OTHER player is written
    820  f0e2							; (`shufflePatterns`), so VDEL does NOT delay by a line on its own — it
    821  f0e2							; moves the landing point to the other register's store cycle.
    822  f0e2							; Measured store phases (`tools/cycle_ledger.py`, P1 worst path):
    823  f0e2							;   COLUP0 c19 (< all pixels: the per-row colour is always this line),
    824  f0e2							;   GRP0 c35, GRP1 c58, COLUP1 c65.
    825  f0e2							; P0: VDELP0=1 moves its landing from GRP0's c35 (= correct art only for
    826  f0e2							;   X < 44 px) to GRP1's c58 (X < 113 px) and, in the same stroke, aligns
    827  f0e2							;   the art with PlayerColTable (today art row r sits one line above its
    828  f0e2							;   colour for X >= 44). P1 keep VDELP1=0: its latch would be GRP0's c35,
    829  f0e2							;   i.e. a WORSE split than today's c58, and P1's colour would stay at c65.
    830  f0e2							; Every .Line body writes GRP1 exactly once on every path (.Grp1 in-window
    831  f0e2							; or .ObjNoRes blank), so the P0 latch is driven every scanline; that is
    832  f0e2							; the contract `tools/test_vdel_cave.py` guards. HERO clears both bits at
    833  f0e2							; cave entry and uses VDEL only for its HUD text, so this is the one place
    834  f0e2							; we deliberately differ (measured, not guessed).
    835  f0e2							; --- Gameplay runs the bank6 cave kernel (tools/cave_kernel_gen.py: one band
    836  f0e2							; code run 4x, branch-free sprite fetch, no dead lines at the band changes).
    837  f0e2							; The title keeps THIS bank's kernel for its band 0 (+ bank1's TitleBand).
    838  f0e2							; `sta $1FFA` selects bank6; the next fetch (the byte after the sta) comes from
    839  f0e2							; bank6 = `jmp Kernel6Entry`; the title branch lands on that same byte in bank0.
    840  f0e2		       a5 8a		      lda	DropTarget
    841  f0e4		       c9 ff		      cmp	#$FF
    842  f0e6		       f0 03		      beq	.TitleKernel
    843  f0e8				   GoKernel6
    844  f0e8		       8d fa 1f 	      sta	BK_CAVE
    845  f0eb				   .TitleKernel
    846  f0eb		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    847  f0ed		       85 25		      sta	VDELP0
    848  f0ef		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    849  f0f1		       85 26		      sta	VDELP1
    850  f0f3		       85 1f		      sta	ENABL	; HUD-bar leftover off before first visible
    851  f0f5							;   line (.Row row0 BandTab rewrites next)
