    952  f123							; --- Phase 5: is the second GRP1 object in THIS band? ---------------
    953  f123							; Sits in the setup window's free tail (~59c after PF2, before the WSYNC
    954  f123							; that ends the pass, so the phased stores above never move). The early
    955  f123							; out costs 5c; Slot1Hook pays 2 extra lines ONLY on the band that hosts
    956  f123							; slot 1 (SetObjectXPos WSYNC line + the HMOVE line).
    957  f123		       a5 ea		      lda	ObjBase1	; $FF = none. `bmi` is still valid HERE (slot 1
    958  f125		       30 03		      bmi	Slot1Keep	;   only holds an enemy design or the miner,
    959  f127							;   all < $80; the bomb never reaches slot 1).
    960  f127							;   Slot 0 must use `cmp #$FF` — see .SODone.
    961  f127		       4c 60 f7 	      jmp	Slot1Hook	; NOT jsr: when the hook positions P1 it owns
    962  f12a							;   the rest of this band (counts its own lines
    963  f12a							;   and jumps into .Line), so a pushed return
    964  f12a							;   address would leak 2 bytes every frame.
    965  f12a							;   Its early-out jumps back to .RowNoSlot1.
    966  f12a				   Slot1Keep
    967  f12a							; (2026-10-15) GRP0 blank REMOVED: +5c pushed the rows0/1 setup
    968  f12a							; segment to 75c armed (>=74 = write lands next line = +1 stall line
    969  f12a							; = whole-screen shift). The blank only traded a stale-byte duplicate
    970  f12a							; for a blank line at band boundaries — shipped pre-99b8e86 without
    971  f12a							; either; case15 filters zero writes so the Y-align guard is unaffected.
    972  f12a							; --- Scanlines this pass (N=4): bands 0-2 = 36; band 3 = 24+off (tide,
    973  f12a							; CollisionX). The bottom water strip (last 12-off lines,
    974  f12a							; bottom_band_plan rule 2) renders in .WaterRow after this pass — its own
    975  f12a							; setup line + (12-off) bodies, so the bottom band spans 38 picture lines
    976  f12a							; and the cave body count is exactly CAVE_LINES (144).
    977  f12a							; Split tail (2026-10-05, row1 setup gap 77->74): the non-bottom gate used
    978  f12a							; to pay `bne` 3c to skip the tide load AND share the WSYNC — gap was 77
    979  f12a							; (stall, +1 line/frame). Non-bottom bands now store+WSYNC before the tide
    980  f12a							; block, then jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line =
    981  f12a							; 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC = 72 <=76). Bottom-band path byte-identical in cost
    982  f12a							; (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    983  f12a							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    984  f12a							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
