   3634  fbfc							; 2026-10-20 (chunk 4): the corridor pads are SPLIT across the banks, exactly
   3635  fbfc							; like the tail pads below. A bank0 caller runs `sta $1FFx` AT A; the next
   3636  fbfc							; opcode fetch (A+3) already comes from the TARGET bank, which keeps only the
   3637  fbfc							; `jmp` half. Nothing in bank1/bank2/bank3 calls a CallPad (only `jmp
   3638  fbfc							; ReturnPad`), so bank0's `jmp` halves and the target banks' `sta` halves were
   3639  fbfc							; dead bytes — packing the live halves reclaimed 70 B of code (bank0 −33,
   3640  fbfc							; bank1 −37). The whole block is still 0 push / 0 cycles: `sta` changes no
   3641  fbfc							; register, no flag, no stack byte.
