   4453  fe90							; FoldIndirect — cross-bank data fetch (HERO fold, write-triggered;
   4454  fe90							; level_bank_plan §0.1). Pad lands $FEF6-$FEFF (last byte ≤ $FEFF — $FF00
   4455  fe90							; stays the fineAdjust anchor). Bytes must be byte-identical in bank2
   4456  fe90							; (guard: verify_build) — after `sta $1FF6` the CPU fetches the remainder
   4457  fe90							; from the data bank at the same PC.
   4458  fe90							; Contract: bank select is ABSOLUTE $1FF6 (bank2) — X/Y both preserved,
   4459  fe90							; A = junk in, data out (`sta $1FF4` switches back, A preserved).
   4460  fe90							; P3.1 deviation (plan §0): `sta $1FF6,X` required X=0, but every enemy
   4461  fe90							; loop keeps the slot in X and has no free temp to swap (DEY/snake hold
   4462  fe90							; Temp live across the read). All level data is bank2, so X-selection is
   4463  fe90							; dead weight; bank3 data later needs a second entry `sta $1FF7` pad.
   4464  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4465  fe90							; E4 moth entry tramp ($FEF0-$FEF5) — byte-identical with bank2's copy
   4466  fe90							; (guard: verify_build check_moth_tramp). bank0 executes `sta $1FF6`; the next
   4467  fe90							; fetch ($FEF3) comes from bank2 = `jmp MothRoutine`. Neither bank runs its
   4468  fe90							; other half: bank0 is switched away at $FEF2, bank2 is never entered here.
   4469  fe90							; The 6-byte pad is the only free hole before FoldIndirect's pinned $FEF6.
   4470  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
